Z||000007||DJRice||07-19-2000||02:33 PM||||If you go to a place that does mufflers, it should be no problem...As long as someone does not get very careless with the welder, the gas tank wont bother you.  Most people have the Catalytic Converters or a straight pipe welded in place when the have exhaust problems down there...<P>Get it welded...You wont have a problem.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
Z||000008||penetrator||07-20-2000||06:23 AM||||DJRice:<P>Okey, i'll do that. And hopefully the car is running much smoother agian.<P>Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||07-20-2000||07:13 PM||||Go to a muffler shop and get it welded. I agree, that's the best way to fix it.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 07-20-2000).]||||reg||1
